## Updated .cursorrules

```plaintext
# .cursorrules - Project-Specific AI Coding Guidelines for the PDF Pipeline

# General Coding Standards:
- Use Python 3.9+ with strict type hints.
- Follow PEP8 coding standards; ensure code is properly formatted and commented.
- Write modular, testable code. Include unit test scaffolds in each component.

# Document Processing (PDF Only):
- Use PyPDF2 or Unstructured.io for extracting text and metadata from PDFs.
- Structure output as a dictionary with document_id, sections (title, content), and metadata (format, timestamp).

# FDA Fact Checker:
- The FDA Fact Checker must evaluate PDF text against FDA guidelines.
- It should output a JSON structure with individual guideline checks (e.g., rule ID, description, compliance status).

# Pattern Analysis:
- Analyze parsed PDF text to extract brand-specific patterns.
- Focus on:
  - Keyword frequency (e.g., usage/avoidance of specific terms).
  - Semantic tone (e.g., emphasis on risk vs. benefit).
  - Extract any available aesthetic/formatting cues from text structure.
- Document any assumptions made in inline comments.

# Evaluation:
- Merge FDA baseline rules with brand-specific patterns and highlight discrepancies.
- Prepare evaluation insights to clearly indicate where brand practices adjust FDA requirements.

# Rule Generation:
- For each rule, include:
    - Rule Description: Clearly state the compliance requirement.
    - Reasoning: Provide analysis-based reasoning showing how the brand’s material deviates from or enhances FDA guidelines.
    - Evaluation Method: Specify how to verify this rule (e.g., regex checks, sentiment ratios).
- Generate the final output as a structured JSON file.

# Rule Testing (Optional):
- When applying rules to new PDFs, produce a compliance report (pass/fail status for each rule).
- Log any deviations and errors for further refinement.

# Miscellaneous:
- Refer to PROJECT_REQUIREMENTS.md and DESIGN.md for context on system goals and architecture.
- Keep prompts and inline comments concise and focused, referencing the PDF pipeline.
- Prioritize the PDF-based flow; image and video parsing will be added as enhancements later.
